+## New features
+
+- `options(gsDesign.quadrature = "gl")` selects Gauss-Legendre quadrature on
+  the continuation region of each analysis for all boundary crossing
+  probability computations (`gsDesign()`, `gsProbability()`, `gsBound()`,
+  `gsBound1()`, `gsDensity()` and everything built on them). The number of
+  nodes adapts to the width of the region relative to the information
+  increment to the next analysis, and `r` acts as a multiplier of the node
+  count. Compared with the default Jennison and Turnbull grid (`"jt"`,
+  unchanged) this is several times faster and about four orders of magnitude
+  more accurate (errors around 1e-12 instead of 1e-7 against exact
+  multivariate normal probabilities), including for many analyses, closely
+  spaced analyses and large drift. Results differ from the default by no more
+  than the accuracy of the default grid. See the "Numerical integration"
+  section of `?gsDesign`.
+
 ## Performance
 
 - The C routines behind `gsBound()`, `gsBound1()`, `gsProbability()`,
